WEBVTT

00:03.310 --> 00:06.230
Rentt, if you're going to live here in Maalt,

00:06.230 --> 00:09.440
you absolutely cannot refuse 
a request from the Latours.

00:10.130 --> 00:11.970
I have no intention of refusing.

00:11.970 --> 00:15.020
But... is it okay?

00:15.950 --> 00:18.500
Um... you're...

00:19.380 --> 00:23.290
<i>If they find out I'm a 
monster, they'll kill me.</i>

00:23.700 --> 00:25.850
It's going to be hard.

00:25.850 --> 00:32.260
No, when I met Isaac, he didn't 
seem to care about my appearance.

00:32.260 --> 00:35.130
If it was an issue, he wouldn't 
have made the request at all.

00:36.970 --> 00:38.320
All right.

00:38.320 --> 00:41.250
But if there's any problem at all, tell me.

00:41.250 --> 00:44.830
Of course. I'll start 
by paying them a visit.

00:56.120 --> 00:58.550
This place is incredible...

01:01.110 --> 01:05.740
<i>I like to think I have a good 
sense of direction, but...</i>

01:08.500 --> 01:10.320
Hmm...

01:11.010 --> 01:15.370
The sun won't help you. I suppose 
that's enough of a hint.

01:16.350 --> 01:19.680
<i>There are very few places in the 
labyrinths where you can see the sun.</i>

01:20.020 --> 01:22.330
<i>Even without the sun to 
guide them, an adventurer</i>

01:22.330 --> 01:24.640
<i>can draw a mental map to guide them.</i>

01:25.000 --> 01:29.750
<i>But if the map in my head was right, I 
would've made it to the exit a long time ago...</i>

01:39.910 --> 01:42.480
This isn't the exit, I suppose.

01:49.950 --> 01:51.710
Will you give up?

01:52.390 --> 01:56.640
No, I'm going to keep 
trying a little longer.

01:56.640 --> 01:58.110
Or is that not okay?

01:58.110 --> 02:00.600
Head that way, then.

02:00.940 --> 02:04.090
Be warned, though, that the maze 
will continue for a while.

02:04.450 --> 02:11.100
If you'd like to take a break, why 
don't you join me for a spot of tea?

02:12.090 --> 02:13.980
I'll do that, then.

03:45.910 --> 03:50.080
<b>The Garden
Labyrinth</b>

03:48.430 --> 03:51.720
<i>I assume she's a daughter 
of the Latour family, then?</i>

03:52.550 --> 03:55.980
<i>The teapot she's using is a 
magic item, as well, I think...</i>

03:57.760 --> 04:01.260
I'm sorry, but did you forget 
to put in the tea leaves?

04:05.050 --> 04:11.510
This teapot can recreate the taste of any 
tea that it's ever been used to brew.

04:11.510 --> 04:14.990
That's an incredible item. 
Where did you get it?

04:15.430 --> 04:18.270
There are two types of magic items: 
ones from the labyrinths,

04:18.270 --> 04:21.440
and those made by craftsmen 
to imitate the former.

04:21.720 --> 04:25.910
This one was discovered 200 
years ago in the labyrinths.

04:25.910 --> 04:30.300
I believe it was worth around 300 platinum.

04:30.300 --> 04:32.030
Platinum?

04:32.490 --> 04:35.220
<i>You could live a lifetime off of just one 
platinum coin and have money left over!</i>

04:35.220 --> 04:37.040
<i>And it cost 300 of them?</i>

04:37.040 --> 04:40.130
The Latour family is a lot wealthier 
than most nobles, then...

04:40.540 --> 04:43.110
It's more than worth it.

04:43.110 --> 04:48.140
Adventurers risked their lives 
in the labyrinths to find it.

04:48.660 --> 04:50.710
You can risk your life in the labyrinths

04:50.710 --> 04:53.480
and only end up with a bunch 
of weird junk, though, too.

04:57.310 --> 04:58.500
This is good!

04:58.850 --> 05:01.280
I'm glad you like it.

05:01.280 --> 05:05.830
I've recreated a tea I had long ago,
the one whose taste I liked best.

05:05.830 --> 05:07.260
I see...

05:07.260 --> 05:09.520
I've never had tea this good.

05:11.040 --> 05:15.400
This may be rude, but is that 
mask also a magic item?

05:15.400 --> 05:16.160
Yeah...

05:16.820 --> 05:18.900
I knew it!

05:18.900 --> 05:21.120
Where did you get it?

05:21.410 --> 05:24.170
Someone I know bought it from 
a street stall in Maalt.

05:24.800 --> 05:27.130
<i>And for three bronze.</i>

05:27.130 --> 05:30.250
I had no idea there was something so 
fascinating to be found in Maalt.

05:30.250 --> 05:33.660
I'm sorry to ask, but...

05:34.100 --> 05:36.150
Would you be willing to part with it?

05:36.640 --> 05:40.500
<i>I heard the Latours collect magic items.</i>

05:40.500 --> 05:42.000
<i>Does she collect them, too?</i>

05:43.400 --> 05:47.370
I'm sorry. It's a valuable item, yes?

05:47.370 --> 05:50.960
Of course, I'm more than willing 
to pay what it's worth.

05:51.860 --> 05:52.980
<i>I'd love to sell it!</i>

05:52.980 --> 05:54.650
<i>If I could only take it off...</i>

05:54.980 --> 06:00.960
<i>But it's only thanks to this mask 
that nobody can see I'm undead.</i>

06:01.470 --> 06:02.810
I'm sorry.

06:02.810 --> 06:04.920
I can't do that.

06:04.920 --> 06:08.970
No, I'm sure it must be an item 
of great importance to you.

06:09.420 --> 06:12.390
It was rude to ask.

06:12.730 --> 06:15.360
No, don't worry about it.

06:17.980 --> 06:19.550
Thank you for the tea.

06:20.230 --> 06:22.050
Take care, then.

06:22.050 --> 06:23.720
Yeah, thanks.

06:24.900 --> 06:27.320
I'll give you a hint.

06:28.040 --> 06:29.320
A hint?

06:30.020 --> 06:32.840
You should avoid looking 
at the sun, perhaps.

06:33.290 --> 06:35.210
The sun, again?

06:35.720 --> 06:37.150
I'll remember that.

06:46.000 --> 06:50.040
<i>There's definitely some trick to this maze.</i>

06:53.370 --> 06:55.230
<i>The sun, huh?</i>

07:04.480 --> 07:05.860
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

07:09.490 --> 07:11.200
<i>Teleportation?</i>

07:11.840 --> 07:13.660
<i>Can you go back?</i>

07:13.660 --> 07:17.000
<i>No, there might be one-way teleporters.</i>

07:17.890 --> 07:22.060
<i>I'm not even in a labyrinth... So 
how could there be traps like this?</i>

07:22.060 --> 07:23.520
<i>Which means...</i>

07:24.120 --> 07:26.590
<i>I'm starting over?</i>

07:41.870 --> 07:43.740
<i>I'm finally out.</i>

07:44.150 --> 07:45.740
Congratulations.

07:47.260 --> 07:50.560
It seems you found the secret of the maze.

07:51.270 --> 07:54.090
It's thanks to the advice 
a certain someone gave me.

07:55.450 --> 08:00.290
I'm Laura Latour, the head 
of the Latour family.

08:00.290 --> 08:02.650
A pleasure to make your acquaintance.

08:03.190 --> 08:05.340
<i>She's the head of the family?</i>

08:05.970 --> 08:09.330
I'm Rentt Vivie. A Bronze-class adventurer.

08:09.910 --> 08:12.090
I came to discuss a job.

08:12.550 --> 08:13.440
And...

08:14.480 --> 08:16.970
I completed the maze.

08:18.330 --> 08:19.980
Indeed you did.

08:19.980 --> 08:23.490
Very few are capable of doing so.

08:23.900 --> 08:26.390
Do I get a reward, too?

08:26.390 --> 08:28.500
Of course you do.

08:30.380 --> 08:36.090
Please choose any magic item you want 
from the Latour Family's collection.

08:36.440 --> 08:40.070
Then can you give me the 
one that made that maze?

08:40.350 --> 08:44.780
I'm sorry. I can't do that.

08:45.600 --> 08:46.750
I was kidding.

08:46.750 --> 08:47.980
Oh my.

08:47.980 --> 08:51.430
You made me walk forever in that labyrinth.

08:51.430 --> 08:53.220
It was my way of getting back at you.

08:53.840 --> 08:55.860
You're a fascinating man.

08:58.860 --> 09:00.480
Right this way.

09:13.310 --> 09:18.100
Magic items made by human 
hands are more consistently reliable.

09:18.960 --> 09:24.330
But we can still only make the 
simplest items, like these lights.

09:24.330 --> 09:26.250
They're filled with mystery.

09:26.250 --> 09:28.280
Just like the labyrinths.

09:34.070 --> 09:35.120
Light.

09:40.790 --> 09:42.460
Wow.

09:42.460 --> 09:44.570
These are all magic items?

09:44.570 --> 09:47.850
Yes. It was very difficult to get 
them all cleaned up and organized.

09:47.850 --> 09:52.380
No, that's not what I 
meant... well, kind of.

09:53.070 --> 09:58.810
How are all the labyrinths around 
the world born? Why do they exist?

09:59.820 --> 10:03.980
No one has ever found an answer.

10:04.730 --> 10:06.460
The magic items are the same.

10:07.920 --> 10:13.540
Just as you said, some of them are junk 
that we have little idea how to use.

10:15.990 --> 10:18.160
What is this item?

10:18.160 --> 10:19.760
I don't know.

10:19.760 --> 10:22.440
If you throw it, it will 
continue to bounce forever.

10:23.050 --> 10:25.650
Why did you collect all this stuff?

10:25.650 --> 10:27.180
Because I wanted it.

10:27.670 --> 10:30.270
That's what it means to 
be an obsessive collector.

10:31.110 --> 10:32.470
I see.

10:32.990 --> 10:34.130
And this?

10:34.460 --> 10:38.690
Have you ever seen the airships 
they have in the west?

10:39.390 --> 10:44.410
They're huge, and carry people 
with the power of steam.

10:44.410 --> 10:46.690
I've heard rumors.

10:46.690 --> 10:50.730
It's a model of one of them. 
It's powered by mana.

10:51.300 --> 10:53.200
You can control it with this.

11:02.060 --> 11:03.730
Is it fun?

11:03.730 --> 11:05.710
Yes. I want it.

11:05.710 --> 11:08.010
Then will you choose this?

11:09.550 --> 11:13.730
<i>I want it, but it's a toy, right?</i>

11:13.730 --> 11:18.040
<i>The young boy inside me wants it, but...</i>

11:18.040 --> 11:22.160
<i>The grown up inside me wants 
something more useful.</i>

11:23.600 --> 11:25.920
You seem hesitant.

11:25.920 --> 11:29.410
Rentt, focus your mind on the model.

11:34.040 --> 11:35.480
What is this?

11:36.600 --> 11:38.360
Amazing, is it not?

11:38.360 --> 11:41.760
The controller can transfer 
their mind into the model.

11:41.760 --> 11:44.360
Yes, that's amazing...

11:44.360 --> 11:46.560
But it burns a lot of mana.

11:46.560 --> 11:49.170
I call it a "model", for 
lack of a better term,

11:49.170 --> 11:51.770
but this was discovered in the labyrinths.

11:52.220 --> 11:53.720
Which means...

11:53.720 --> 11:58.340
Yes. The airships are 
modeled after this item.

11:58.920 --> 12:01.850
Though they could never 
figure out what made it fly,

12:01.850 --> 12:04.210
and were forced to turn to other means.

12:04.210 --> 12:07.050
I thought it was just a toy...

12:07.920 --> 12:10.670
But it would be very helpful for scouting.

12:10.670 --> 12:11.680
Yes.

12:11.680 --> 12:16.540
But because of the way it uses mana, 
you can't send it that far ahead.

12:16.540 --> 12:17.920
True.

12:17.920 --> 12:21.190
It couldn't go more than a 
few minutes with my magic.

12:21.190 --> 12:22.510
What will you do?

12:23.530 --> 12:25.460
I'll think about it.

12:25.460 --> 12:27.940
Take your time, then.

12:27.940 --> 12:29.690
I will.

12:31.410 --> 12:34.050
There's a lot ahead too, isn't there?

12:36.680 --> 12:38.340
Is this a magic item as well?

12:38.340 --> 12:41.410
Yes. It lights up when something approaches.

12:41.740 --> 12:43.330
Anything?

12:43.330 --> 12:45.780
Yes. It will react even to a rat.

12:45.780 --> 12:48.320
Sounds useful, but I don't know 
if it actually would be...

12:50.870 --> 12:52.990
This seems to be a normal painting.

12:55.750 --> 12:58.690
Press the button on the frame.

12:59.590 --> 13:00.940
This?

13:07.230 --> 13:09.360
Isn't it intriguing?

13:09.360 --> 13:11.960
What do you think those voices are?

13:12.450 --> 13:15.230
<i>Is she just enjoying watching my reactions?</i>

13:19.010 --> 13:21.030
Rentt, be careful!

13:24.870 --> 13:27.240
Isaac, where's the shutdown device?

13:27.240 --> 13:30.940
We put it somewhere else, just to be safe.

13:42.590 --> 13:44.410
<i>You're kidding me...</i>

13:52.730 --> 13:54.490
<i>Why is there a golem here?</i>

14:04.200 --> 14:06.940
<i>Even I couldn't take a 
hit from this thing...</i>

14:06.940 --> 14:08.420
Isaac, hurry!

14:08.420 --> 14:09.660
Yes, of course.

14:09.660 --> 14:12.100
Rentt, just try and hang 
in there for a while!

14:12.100 --> 14:13.940
It should be around here...

14:13.940 --> 14:16.350
It's important to keep things organized.

14:21.320 --> 14:24.250
Hey, how long can a golem stay powered?

14:24.620 --> 14:27.060
It only took a little bit of my mana!

14:27.060 --> 14:30.270
It only used your mana to activate!

14:30.270 --> 14:34.650
That golem absorbs the mana and inorganic 
matter in its surroundings to become stronger.

14:39.010 --> 14:40.980
Can I hurt it a little?

14:40.980 --> 14:42.300
I don't mind.

14:42.300 --> 14:44.980
But you won't be able 
to defeat it in battle.

14:44.980 --> 14:47.330
I'm not planning on beating it.

14:59.200 --> 15:00.580
Listen to me, Rentt.

15:00.990 --> 15:05.970
Golems have a word in a magical tongue 
on their forehead that means "truth."

15:05.970 --> 15:10.390
You can add a single character 
to change that word to "death,"

15:10.390 --> 15:12.850
which will cause it to collapse.

15:13.410 --> 15:14.720
There's nothing on its forehead at all!

15:21.370 --> 15:24.700
At least, that's how they did 
it in the very early days.

15:24.700 --> 15:27.620
Normally they come with an 
external shutdown device.

15:27.620 --> 15:28.930
And if it doesn't have one?

15:28.930 --> 15:31.940
Then you have to run, or defeat it.

15:32.470 --> 15:34.960
Hey, have you found that shutdown device yet?

15:34.960 --> 15:38.130
I'm pretty sure it was on this shelf...

15:39.250 --> 15:40.910
Well, I can't keep this up any longer.

15:46.330 --> 15:50.800
<i>I didn't want to show anyone this 
technique, but... I have no choice!</i>

15:51.320 --> 15:53.130
<i>Mana-Spirit Fusion will do it!</i>

16:01.030 --> 16:01.660
Halt.

16:07.650 --> 16:09.550
So they made it in time...

16:10.270 --> 16:13.120
I'm so sorry! Are you hurt?

16:13.120 --> 16:14.370
I'm fine.

16:14.950 --> 16:19.540
My failure to properly manage our 
magic items has put you in danger.

16:19.540 --> 16:23.210
No, as your master, it's my fault.

16:23.210 --> 16:27.560
No, it's my fault for carelessly 
touching a magic item.

16:28.720 --> 16:29.920
<i>More importantly...</i>

16:30.740 --> 16:33.200
<i>They're not gonna ask me 
to pay for it, are they?</i>

16:33.970 --> 16:38.100
I'll have the servants clean this up later.

16:38.850 --> 16:41.930
Now, what magic item will you choose?

16:41.930 --> 16:45.510
If you don't mind, I'd like to continue.

16:51.640 --> 16:52.600
What's that?

16:54.820 --> 16:57.280
Materials taken from monsters.

16:57.590 --> 17:02.110
They're not magic items, but they can be used to make medicine and weapons.

17:03.120 --> 17:05.350
Materials taken from monsters?

17:18.130 --> 17:19.850
Does that catch your interest?

17:22.680 --> 17:26.890
It's the blood of a vampire.

17:32.650 --> 17:38.230
Ingesting the blood of a vampire is 
said to make one a vampire themself.

17:38.720 --> 17:40.120
Is that true?

17:40.120 --> 17:41.940
It's just a rumor.

17:42.310 --> 17:46.210
There are quite a few records of 
people drinking vampire blood.

17:46.210 --> 17:49.590
Most of them went mad and died.

17:50.200 --> 17:53.670
The few who survived are said to have become 
hollow shells of their former selves.

17:54.290 --> 17:58.100
So nobody was ever able to 
become a vampire, then?

17:58.100 --> 18:02.510
Do you think anyone would ever 
say they've become a vampire?

18:02.510 --> 18:05.420
They would immediately be killed.

18:05.420 --> 18:06.770
True.

18:06.770 --> 18:08.780
So there's just rumors, and nothing more.

18:09.130 --> 18:14.870
But even rumors are enough to make it 
desired among those who wish for eternal life.

18:14.870 --> 18:18.490
You can sell it for a fortune 
to the high nobility.

18:21.560 --> 18:22.690
I've made my choice.

18:27.060 --> 18:29.510
And this is what you chose?

18:30.090 --> 18:31.210
Yes.

18:31.210 --> 18:33.790
Yes, it's wonderful.

18:40.850 --> 18:46.690
I've seen airships, but I had no idea 
they were inspired by a magic item.

18:51.190 --> 18:56.890
And not only can you control 
it, you can see what it sees?

18:57.760 --> 18:59.370
It's a ton of fun.

18:59.370 --> 19:03.070
Who are the Latour family, though?

19:03.070 --> 19:05.650
They're freer with gifts than many royals.

19:05.650 --> 19:08.760
Well, there aren't many
adventurers like me

19:08.760 --> 19:12.170
who make regular trips 
to the Tarasque swamp.

19:13.760 --> 19:16.220
I can really take this, too?

19:16.220 --> 19:20.350
Yes. It's thanks for taking 
on such a troublesome job.

19:20.350 --> 19:27.010
Of course, we'll pay you what's on the job 
sheet each time you complete the task.

19:27.010 --> 19:28.610
I see.

19:28.610 --> 19:32.300
Now I can devote myself 
fully to caring for Laura.

19:33.360 --> 19:35.970
So, you want to try it?

19:37.170 --> 19:43.090
Of course... but I think first it's 
time to stop playing and face reality.

19:43.650 --> 19:46.340
I wasn't just playing...

20:03.400 --> 20:05.100
Was he to your liking?

20:05.700 --> 20:07.430
Is that how it seems to you?

20:07.430 --> 20:08.390
Yes.

20:08.980 --> 20:11.490
He was a rare sort of guest.

20:11.490 --> 20:13.550
I'm afraid I let myself get too excited.

20:14.230 --> 20:16.060
It was a nice change of pace.

20:16.440 --> 20:20.250
But for now, 
please get some rest.

20:23.880 --> 20:25.830
It's safe to assume this is real?

20:26.420 --> 20:28.460
I'm pretty sure it is.

20:28.460 --> 20:31.880
When I saw this, I could feel it.

20:32.590 --> 20:36.230
If I drink this, I knew, 
something would change.

20:37.450 --> 20:39.990
Something instinctive?

20:39.990 --> 20:41.790
But are you sure?

20:42.250 --> 20:44.750
Just as Laura Latour said,

20:44.750 --> 20:50.940
the records say that everyone who ingests 
vampire blood meets a terrible end...

20:51.980 --> 20:54.050
So it seems.

20:54.050 --> 20:56.190
It's rare for you to be hesitant.

20:56.750 --> 20:59.180
I'd be lying if I said I wasn't scared.

21:00.370 --> 21:03.310
I know I need this if I'm going to evolve.

21:04.410 --> 21:06.560
My body wants it.

21:07.110 --> 21:09.430
But it's too dangerous.

21:09.430 --> 21:11.490
You may not survive.

21:12.470 --> 21:16.370
Even if your undead body can take it, you...

21:18.500 --> 21:21.530
If you can avoid drinking 
it, I'd prefer you don't.

21:22.790 --> 21:27.580
I wouldn't mind you being an undead forever.

21:29.100 --> 21:34.380
Just stay here forever and spend 
your life as an adventurer.

21:35.260 --> 21:36.570
Lorraine...

21:37.230 --> 21:40.440
But that's not what you want, is it?

21:41.150 --> 21:45.030
Even if you don't have the talent, 
even if it takes you years...

21:45.420 --> 21:47.980
You want to become one 
no matter what, right?

21:48.740 --> 21:50.800
A Mythril-class adventurer...

23:35.720 --> 23:39.970
Rentt Faina
